course: dictionary
lesson: 1132
title: Breathless and the words around it
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Breathless is an adjective, and it has more than one meaning. Its first meaning is out of breath, breathing hard after running or effort. In PE, exercise makes you breathless because your muscles need more oxygen.
explain: The word can also mean very excited or amazed. «Breathless with excitement» means so excited that you almost stop breathing. Read the words around it to choose the right meaning: the excitement tells you which one fits.
explain: Aanya in Singapore asks why an author writes «and then, and then» so often. Sometimes it is on purpose: it can make a narrator sound young and breathless. «Like that one» is Singapore English for «in that way», so the question means why the author writes in that way.
explain: Breathless can also describe air or weather that is still, with no wind. In «a breathless hush», the word shows a silence so still that everyone seems to hold their breath. If you feel breathless for no reason, tell an adult, because it can be a sign of illness or asthma.
fact: Breathless means out of breath, breathing hard after running or effort.
fact: «Breathless with excitement» means very excited, so that you almost stop breathing.
fact: «A breathless hush» means a very still, quiet silence.
fact: Feeling breathless for no reason can be a sign of illness or asthma, so tell an adult.
fact: Singapore English «like that one» means in that way.
exercise: What does «breathless with excitement» mean? | *So excited that you almost stop breathing | Cold and wet | Out of breath after running | Angry and shouting
exercise: Aanya asks why an author writes «and then, and then». What can this repeated phrase do? | It shows the narrator is a teacher | It is a spelling mistake that must be fixed | It means the story is very short | *It can make a narrator sound young and breathless
exercise: In PE, why does exercise make you breathless? | The gym is too quiet | *Your muscles need more oxygen | You have eaten too much cake
test:
What does «a breathless hush» suggest? | Loud cheering from the crowd | A strong wind blowing hard | *A very still, quiet silence
What should you do if you feel breathless for no reason? | Keep running until it stops | Ignore it, because it is normal | *Tell an adult, since it can be a sign of illness or asthma | Laugh about it and forget it
exam: Which meaning of breathless fits best in «a breathless hush», and what clue helps you choose? | Cold, because it is winter | Very angry, because someone shouted | Out of breath, because someone ran | *Still and silent, because a hush is quiet
